# 1-based lines to bookmark. Each sits INSIDE a construct the profile claims to
# understand, so a broken `containers` shows up as a missing breadcrumb.
#
# The sample uses the BRACED namespace form, which changes what this file can
# assert. `namespace App\Billing;` (semicolon) encloses nothing in the AST, so
# it could never appear in a breadcrumb — the old sample used it and recorded
# that as a permanent gap. With `namespace App\Billing { ... }` the namespace is
# a real ancestor, so every trail below is one level deeper and
# `namespace_definition` is an observed container rather than a curated guess.

# Inside a method on an enum — proves `enum_declaration` is a container, which
# only works because the enum holds a method and not just cases.
33

# Inside a method on a trait. PHP's unit of reuse, and a container kind the old
# sample never reached.
50

# Inside the constructor's guard clause: namespace > class > constructor.
101

# Inside a match arm inside the foreach in total() — the deepest chain here:
# namespace > class > method > foreach > match > arm. The four match fragments
# (`match_block`, `match_condition_list`, `match_conditional_expression`,
# `match_default_expression`) are deliberately unlabelled, so the breadcrumb
# names the method rather than the arm.
116

# Inside the try block in pay(), which also has catch and finally.
127

# Inside jsonSerialize(), on the line opening a closure assigned to a variable.
146

# Inside isVoid() on `final class LineItem`, a separate class in the namespace.
175

# Inside the top-level function formatMoney() — proves `function_definition`
# works as a container with the namespace above it.
181

# Inside the `if` inside the foreach in the generator function eachTaxable().
191
